        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;*1 &lt;b&gt;Security groups for AWS resources&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;SG app allows egress only to 443 on the S3 prefix list and 8080 on the server's SG. S3 Access Points worked; 443 and 2049 to the SVM did not. The same held for an isolated pod.&lt;br&gt;*2 &lt;b&gt;NetworkPolicy between Pods&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The server accepts 8080 only from role=client. A Pod with no SecurityGroupPolicy was stopped by the server's SG even though the NetworkPolicy allowed it.&lt;br&gt;*3 &lt;b&gt;Trident PVs are outside the Pod's SG&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The node mounts NFS. A Pod whose SG allows no egress still wrote to its PV.&lt;br&gt;*4 &lt;b&gt;Scope&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;2026-11-12, ap-northeast-1a, one observation each. Pod icons are Kubernetes community icons (Apache-2.0)." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=24;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;strokeColor=#232F3E;fillColor=none;fontColor=#232F3E;fontSize=16;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="580" width="920" height="260" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
